### Case: correlation-id-present — an authenticated call.
### Expect 200 AND an X-Request-Id response header.
###
### Capture the X-Request-Id value: you need it for the correlation-end-to-end case,
### which is where the actual value of a correlation id lives. Presence at the
### gateway is necessary and not sufficient — your backend has to log it too.
GET {{GATEWAY}}/orders
authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
accept: application/json

### curl, showing headers so you can grab the id:
###   curl -i {{GATEWAY}}/orders -H 'authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}'
